## ASP.NET Core Fundamentals <a name="fundamentals"></a>

### 1. Project Structure & Purpose

```
MyWebApp/
├── Controllers/              # Handle HTTP requests & return responses
│   ├── HomeController.cs      # Pages & general navigation
│   ├── ProductController.cs   # Product-related operations
│   └── AccountController.cs   # Authentication & user management
├── Views/                    # HTML templates (MVC pattern)
│   ├── Home/
│   │   ├── Index.cshtml      # Home page template
│   │   └── About.cshtml      # About page template
│   └── Shared/
│       ├── _Layout.cshtml    # Master layout (header, footer, nav)
│       └── _ViewStart.cshtml # Applied to every view
├── Models/                   # Data models & view models
│   ├── Product.cs            # Database entity
│   ├── ProductViewModel.cs   # UI-specific model
│   └── User.cs
├── Services/                 # Business logic layer
│   ├── IProductService.cs    # Interface (contract)
│   └── ProductService.cs     # Implementation
├── Data/
│   ├── ApplicationDbContext.cs  # Entity Framework DbContext
│   └── DbInitializer.cs         # Seed initial data
├── wwwroot/                  # Static files (CSS, JS, images)
│   ├── css/
│   ├── js/
│   └── images/
├── appsettings.json          # Configuration file
├── appsettings.Development.json
├── Program.cs                # Entry point & service registration
├── Startup.cs                # (Optional in .NET 6+)
└── MyWebApp.csproj          # Project file with dependencies
```

**Theory:** This separation of concerns makes code maintainable, testable, and scalable.

### 2. Program.cs (Entry Point) - Complete Example

```csharp
// Entry point: Runs before anything else
// Purpose: Configure all services and middleware

var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);

// ============================================
// PHASE 1: ADD SERVICES (Dependency Container)
// ============================================

// Controllers with Views (for MVC)
builder.Services.AddControllersWithViews();

// Or just API Controllers
// builder.Services.AddControllers();

// Database Context (ORM Layer)
builder.Services.AddDbContext<ApplicationDbContext>(options =>
    options.UseSqlServer(
        builder.Configuration.GetConnectionString("DefaultConnection")));

// Business Logic Services
builder.Services.AddScoped<IProductService, ProductService>();
builder.Services.AddScoped<ICategoryService, CategoryService>();
builder.Services.AddScoped<IUserService, UserService>();

// Utilities
builder.Services.AddScoped<IEmailService, EmailService>();
builder.Services.AddScoped<ILogger, ConsoleLogger>();

// Caching
builder.Services.AddMemoryCache();
builder.Services.AddStackExchangeRedisCache(options =>
    options.Configuration = builder.Configuration.GetConnectionString("Redis"));

// Authentication & Authorization
builder.Services.AddAuthentication(CookieAuthenticationDefaults.AuthenticationScheme)
    .AddCookie(options =>
    {
        options.LoginPath = "/Account/Login";
        options.LogoutPath = "/Account/Logout";
    });

builder.Services.AddAuthorization(options =>
{
    options.AddPolicy("AdminOnly", policy => policy.RequireRole("Admin"));
    options.AddPolicy("CanEdit", policy => policy.RequireClaim("Permission", "Edit"));
});

// CORS for API access from different domains
builder.Services.AddCors(options =>
{
    options.AddPolicy("AllowAll", builder =>
        builder.AllowAnyOrigin().AllowAnyMethod().AllowAnyHeader());
});

// Swagger/OpenAPI Documentation
builder.Services.AddEndpointsApiExplorer();
builder.Services.AddSwaggerGen();

// Session management
builder.Services.AddSession(options =>
{
    options.IdleTimeout = TimeSpan.FromMinutes(30);
});

// ============================================
// Build the application
// ============================================
var app = builder.Build();

// ============================================
// PHASE 2: CONFIGURE MIDDLEWARE (Request Pipeline)
// ============================================

// Development only
if (app.Environment.IsDevelopment())
{
    app.UseDeveloperExceptionPage();
    app.UseSwagger();
    app.UseSwaggerUI();
}
else
{
    // Production: Custom error page
    app.UseExceptionHandler("/Home/Error");
    // Add security headers
    app.UseHsts();
}

// HTTPS redirection (redirect HTTP to HTTPS)
app.UseHttpsRedirection();

// Serve static files (CSS, JS, images from wwwroot)
app.UseStaticFiles();

// Session middleware
app.UseSession();

// Routing: Match URL to controller/action
app.UseRouting();

// CORS: Allow cross-origin requests
app.UseCors("AllowAll");

// Authentication: Identify the user
app.UseAuthentication();

// Authorization: Check permissions
app.UseAuthorization();

// ============================================
// PHASE 3: MAP ENDPOINTS (Define routes)
// ============================================

// MVC Routes
app.MapControllerRoute(
    name: "default",
    pattern: "{controller=Home}/{action=Index}/{id?}");

// Or API Routes
// app.MapControllers();

// ============================================
// START APPLICATION
// ============================================
app.Run();  // This starts the Kestrel server and listens for requests
```

**Theory Explanation:**
- **Program.cs Flow:** 1) Create builder → 2) Register services → 3) Build app → 4) Configure middleware → 5) Map endpoints → 6) Run
- **Services (DI Container):** Store all dependencies before app starts
- **Middleware:** Each middleware processes request, possibly modifies it, then passes to next middleware
- **Endpoints:** Final destination that handles the request

### 3. Practical Startup Configuration (Older Pattern)

```csharp
// For .NET 5 and earlier (explicit Startup class)
public class Startup
{
    public IConfiguration Configuration { get; }
    
    public Startup(IConfiguration configuration)
    {
        Configuration = configuration;
    }
    
    // Called by runtime to add services to DI container
    public void ConfigureServices(IServiceCollection services)
    {
        // Register dependencies here
        services.AddControllers();
        
        // Database
        services.AddDbContext<ApplicationDbContext>(options =>
            options.UseSqlServer(Configuration.GetConnectionString("Default")));
        
        // Services
        services.AddScoped<IUserService, UserService>();
        services.AddScoped<IProductService, ProductService>();
    }
    
    // Called by runtime to configure HTTP request pipeline
    public void Configure(IApplicationBuilder app, IWebHostEnvironment env)
    {
        // This order matters!
        
        if (env.IsDevelopment())
        {
            app.UseDeveloperExceptionPage();
        }
        else
        {
            app.UseExceptionHandler("/Home/Error");
            app.UseHsts();
        }
        
        app.UseHttpsRedirection();
        app.UseStaticFiles();  // wwwroot folder
        
        app.UseRouting();
        
        app.UseEndpoints(endpoints =>
        {
            endpoints.MapControllerRoute(
                name: "default",
                pattern: "{controller=Home}/{action=Index}/{id?}");
        });
    }
}

// In Program.cs (minimal):
public class Program
{
    public static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        CreateHostBuilder(args).Build().Run();
    }
    
    public static IHostBuilder CreateHostBuilder(string[] args) =>
        Host.CreateDefaultBuilder(args)
            .ConfigureWebHostDefaults(webBuilder =>
            {
                webBuilder.UseStartup<Startup>();
            });
}
```

**Key Concepts:**
- `ConfigureServices`: Add services (DI registration)
- `Configure`: Setup middleware pipeline
- Order matters: Middleware is executed in registration order
```

