### Q6: Explain the difference between DbContext.SaveChanges() and SaveChangesAsync().

**Answer:**
- **SaveChanges()**: Synchronous, blocks thread
- **SaveChangesAsync()**: Asynchronous, releases thread

**Use async in:**
- Web applications (better scalability)
- I/O-bound operations
- Cloud environments

```csharp
// Synchronous
public void CreateProduct(Product product)
{
    _context.Products.Add(product);
    _context.SaveChanges();  // Blocks thread
}

// Asynchronous (preferred)
public async Task CreateProductAsync(Product product)
{
    _context.Products.Add(product);
    await _context.SaveChangesAsync();  // Non-blocking
}
```

