## Best Practices Checklist

### Code Organization
- [ ] Controllers only handle HTTP concerns
- [ ] Business logic in Services layer
- [ ] Data access in Repository layer
- [ ] Models defined separately from DTOs
- [ ] Use interfaces for dependencies

### Performance
- [ ] Use async/await for all I/O operations
- [ ] Implement caching for frequently accessed data
- [ ] Use pagination for large result sets
- [ ] Include `.Include()` to prevent N+1 queries
- [ ] Create indexes on frequently queried columns

### Security
- [ ] Validate all user input
- [ ] Use HTTPS for all endpoints
- [ ] Implement authentication (JWT, OAuth2)
- [ ] Implement authorization (roles, policies)
- [ ] Sanitize data before displaying
- [ ] Use parameterized queries (EF Core does this)
- [ ] Never log sensitive information
- [ ] Implement rate limiting

### Error Handling
- [ ] Use global exception middleware
- [ ] Log exceptions with context
- [ ] Return meaningful HTTP status codes
- [ ] Don't expose internal errors to client
- [ ] Validate model state in controllers

### Testing
- [ ] Write unit tests for services
- [ ] Use mocks for dependencies
- [ ] Test both happy path and error cases
- [ ] Aim for 70%+ code coverage
- [ ] Use integration tests for databases

### Documentation
- [ ] Document API endpoints with Swagger
- [ ] Add XML comments to public methods
- [ ] Update README with setup instructions
- [ ] Document database schema changes
- [ ] Add examples to complex business logic

### Deployment
- [ ] Use environment variables for config
- [ ] Don't hardcode secrets
- [ ] Use connection string encryption
- [ ] Implement health checks
- [ ] Set up automated backups
- [ ] Use Docker for containerization
- [ ] Implement CI/CD pipeline

