## Performance Optimization Tips

### 1. Database Optimization
```csharp
// ❌ Slow: Retrieves all, filters in memory
var products = _context.Products.ToList()
    .Where(p => p.Price > 100)
    .ToList();

// ✅ Fast: Filters at database level
var products = await _context.Products
    .Where(p => p.Price > 100)
    .ToListAsync();
```

### 2. Caching
```csharp
// ✅ Cache frequently accessed data
var cacheKey = "top_products";
if (!_cache.TryGetValue(cacheKey, out List<Product> products))
{
    products = await _repository.GetTopProductsAsync();
    _cache.Set(cacheKey, products, TimeSpan.FromHours(1));
}
```

### 3. Projection
```csharp
// ❌ Retrieves all columns, wastes memory
var products = await _context.Products.ToListAsync();

// ✅ Retrieves only needed columns
var products = await _context.Products
    .Select(p => new { p.Id, p.Name, p.Price })
    .ToListAsync();
```

### 4. Batching
```csharp
// ✅ Batch operations for efficiency
public async Task InsertManyAsync(IEnumerable<Product> products)
{
    foreach (var batch in products.Batch(100))
    {
        _context.Products.AddRange(batch);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

